      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_1234159" metaid="metaid_65" name="Proteasome proteolyzes ub-HIF-alpha" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Destruction of ubiquitinated HIF-alpha can occur in both the cytosol and nucleus (Berra et al. 2001). Upon reoxygenation of hypoxic cells HIF-alpha is ubiquitinated in the nucleus and transported to the cytosol in a complex with VHL:ElonginB:ElonginC:CUL2:RBX1 where it is destroyed (Groulx and Lee 2002, Jaakkola et al. 2001, Ivan et al. 2001)</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
